+@conformance
+Feature: DOM node identity during state changes
+  As a project maintaining browser-compatible rendering
+  I want DOM nodes to persist across state-changing interactions
+  So that real-browser test runners can hold element references across chained commands
+
+  The app must not destroy and recreate list-item DOM nodes when toggling
+  completion state. A real browser (Cypress, Playwright) obtains a reference
+  to an li element, fires a click on its checkbox, then continues the command
+  chain against that same reference. If render() replaces innerHTML, every
+  prior reference detaches and the chain fails with "element has detached
+  from the DOM". The in-harness Cucumber suite re-queries between steps,
+  so it never observes this detachment. This feature pins DOM identity so
+  the defect is caught at the source level.
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Toggling a single todo preserves the li DOM node identity
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy milk     | false     |
+      | Walk the dog | false     |
+    And the list item references are captured
+    When the user toggles the checkbox for todo "Buy milk"
+    Then every captured list item reference is still attached to the document
+    And the todo "Buy milk" has the completed class
+
+  Scenario: Toggling all todos preserves the li DOM node identity
+    Given the following todos exist:
+      | title        | completed |
+      | Buy milk     | false     |
+      | Walk the dog | false     |
+    And the list item references are captured
+    When the user clicks the toggle-all checkbox
+    Then every captured list item reference is still attached to the document
+    And all todos are completed
